[00:00.48] Boots were of leather
[00:04.56] A breath of cologne
[00:09.70] Her mirror was a window
[00:14.54] She sat quite alone
[00:21.24] All around her
[00:24.62] The garden grew
[00:30.48] Scarlet and purple
[00:34.20] And crimson and blue
[00:40.10] She came and she went
[00:44.74] And at last went away
[00:50.16] The garden was sealed
[00:55.00] When the flowers decayed
[01:01.12] On the wall of the garden
[01:05.02] A legend did say:
[01:11.30] No one may come here
[01:15.32] Since no one may stay
